Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: let a sink request DFP before discovery

A charge-through dock or hub is the power source and wants to be the USB
device.  It attaches as Source/DFP and asks for a DR_Swap once discovery
has run; on the SM-X910 about 270 ms after the last discovery reply.  With
the SM5714 that swap does not hold.  TCPM accepts it and becomes DFP, and
1.3 to 5.7 ms after the Accept the partner sends a Soft_Reset whose header
still claims Source/DFP, whether or not the port has sent anything in its
new role by then.  TCPM logs "Data role mismatch, initiating error
recovery", and the next attach repeats it.  One hub did this 28 times out
of 28; a dock from another vendor did it in one of the two attaches on
record and sent a Hard_Reset in the other.  The cause is unknown.

A DR_Swap that the sink sent before its first Discover Identity was
accepted within 4 ms and held, both times that happened (one hub; the
requests came from user space and happened to get in ahead of discovery).
One that is started later, while a VDM of the port is waiting for its
reply, collides with that reply and ends in a Soft_Reset, 30 times out of
30.  User space cannot time the request; TCPM can, by making it before
discovery.

Provide an opt-in TCPC flag for that.  As Sink/UFP under an explicit
contract, when the first source PDO advertises data role swap, request DFP
from the SNK_READY entry instead of starting discovery.  The request goes
through tcpm_ams_start(), so a PD 3.0 sink still waits for SinkTxOK; when
it has to wait, the discover work retries it before it sends anything of
its own.  No request is made on top of a state change that is already
pending, or once the port has gone on to its own Discover Identity.

Accept, Reject and Not_Supported settle the matter, and so does a data role
swap that the partner asked for and the port accepted, so that the port
does not ask for a role back that it has just handed over.  After Wait the
request is repeated once tDRSwapWait has passed.  A request that got no
answer or was lost to another message is repeated as well.  At most three
requests are started per attach.  After Accept, discovery runs once, as
DFP; otherwise it runs as it does today.

A Hard Reset returns both ends to their default data roles, a host role
that came from a DR_Swap included, and the request is made again after
the new contract if one is left.

DR_SWAP_SEND sets send_discover (as UFP, or above PD 2.0) and
DR_SWAP_SEND_TIMEOUT clears it, which assumes that discovery had already
run.  With the flag set, the timeout restores what DR_SWAP_SEND found: a
request that got no answer is still followed by discovery, and a swap asked
for after discovery is not.

Also with the flag set, the discover work stops re-arming itself once the
port is detached, and a detach or a Hard Reset drops a state change that
was queued before it.  tcpm_ams_start() leaves the request in
upcoming_state until the state machine runs; if the detach or the reset is
handled first, the next SNK_READY would send the DR_Swap unchecked, to
another partner or in a data role it was not meant for.  HARD_RESET_SEND
already clears upcoming_state for a Hard Reset that the port sends.

Ports whose TCPC does not set the flag are not affected.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c | 124 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 include/linux/usb/tcpm.h      |   9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -276,6 +276,10 @@ enum frs_typec_current {
 #define GET_SINK_CAP_RETRY_MS	100
 #define SEND_DISCOVER_RETRY_MS	100
 
+/* tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink: DR_Swap requests per attach, and tDRSwapWait */
+#define SINK_DFP_SWAP_TRIES	3
+#define SINK_DFP_SWAP_WAIT_MS	100
+
 struct pd_mode_data {
 	int svid_index;		/* current SVID index		*/
 	int nsvids;
@@ -531,6 +535,15 @@ struct tcpm_port {
 	unsigned int hard_reset_count;
 	bool pd_capable;
 	bool explicit_contract;
+	/*
+	 * tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink, per attach: the DR_Swap requests started,
+	 * whether requesting is over, and when tDRSwapWait ends.
+	 */
+	unsigned int sink_dfp_tries;
+	bool sink_dfp_done;
+	ktime_t sink_dfp_not_before;
+	/* What send_discover was when the DR_Swap in progress was sent */
+	bool send_discover_before_swap;
 	unsigned int rx_msgid;
 
 	/* USB PD objects */
@@ -1763,6 +1776,62 @@ static int tcpm_ams_start(struct tcpm_po
 }
 
 /*
+ * Opt-in (tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink): as Sink/UFP under an explicit contract
+ * with a Source that advertises data role swap, ask for DFP before discovery
+ * starts.  The request goes out ahead of the port's own Discover Identity, so
+ * that it cannot collide with a VDM that is waiting for its reply, and
+ * discovery runs once, in the resulting role.  Once the port has gone on to
+ * its Discover Identity, no request is made.
+ *
+ * Accept, Reject and Not_Supported settle the matter, and so does a data role
+ * swap that the partner asked for and the port accepted.  After Wait the
+ * request is repeated once tDRSwapWait has passed; a request that got no
+ * answer, or that was lost to another message, is repeated as well.  At most
+ * SINK_DFP_SWAP_TRIES requests are started per attach.  Until the matter is
+ * settled or the requests are used up, no Discover Identity is sent.
+ *
+ * A Hard Reset reopens the matter.  A host role that came from a DR_Swap goes
+ * back to the default there, and a request that was about to go out is
+ * dropped.
+ *
+ * A request waits while the port has a state change pending, which it would
+ * otherwise replace.
+ *
+ * Returns 1 when a DR_Swap was started, -EAGAIN when it has to wait, and 0
+ * when no request is due.
+ */
+static int tcpm_request_dfp_as_sink(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	if (!port->tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink || port->sink_dfp_done ||
+	    port->sink_dfp_tries >= SINK_DFP_SWAP_TRIES)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (port->typec_caps.data != TYPEC_PORT_DRD ||
+	    port->pwr_role != TYPEC_SINK || port->data_role != TYPEC_DEVICE ||
+	    !port->pd_capable || !port->explicit_contract ||
+	    !port->nr_source_caps ||
+	    !(port->source_caps[0] & PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP))
+		return 0;
+
+	if (port->state != SNK_READY || port->vdm_sm_running ||
+	    port->upcoming_state != INVALID_STATE ||
+	    port->delayed_state != INVALID_STATE ||
+	    ktime_before(ktime_get(), port->sink_dfp_not_before))
+		return -EAGAIN;
+
+	port->upcoming_state = DR_SWAP_SEND;
+	if (tcpm_ams_start(port, DATA_ROLE_SWAP) == -EAGAIN) {
+		port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
+		return -EAGAIN;
+	}
+
+	port->sink_dfp_tries++;
+	tcpm_log(port, "Requesting DFP before discovery");
+
+	return 1;
+}
+
+/*
  * VDM/VDO handling functions
  */
 static void tcpm_queue_vdm(struct tcpm_port *port, const u32 header,
@@ -3680,6 +3749,12 @@ static void tcpm_pd_ctrl_request(struct
 		case DR_SWAP_SEND:
 			port->swap_status = (type == PD_CTRL_WAIT ?
 					     -EAGAIN : -EOPNOTSUPP);
+			/* For tcpm_request_dfp_as_sink(): Wait is not final */
+			if (type == PD_CTRL_WAIT)
+				port->sink_dfp_not_before =
+					ktime_add_ms(ktime_get(), SINK_DFP_SWAP_WAIT_MS);
+			else
+				port->sink_dfp_done = true;
 			tcpm_set_state(port, DR_SWAP_CANCEL, 0);
 			break;
 		case PR_SWAP_SEND:
@@ -4956,6 +5031,12 @@ static void tcpm_reset_port(struct tcpm_
 	tcpm_typec_disconnect(port);
 	port->attached = false;
 	port->pd_capable = false;
+	port->sink_dfp_tries = 0;
+	port->sink_dfp_done = false;
+	port->sink_dfp_not_before = 0;
+	/* A request that was about to go out is not for the next partner */
+	if (port->tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink)
+		port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
 	port->pps_data.supported = false;
 	tcpm_set_partner_usb_comm_capable(port, false);
 
@@ -5853,7 +5934,13 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcp
 				port->tx_sop_type = TCPC_TX_SOP;
 				tcpm_set_initial_svdm_version(port);
 			}
-			mod_send_discover_delayed_work(port, 0);
+			/*
+			 * A DR_Swap requested here precedes discovery, which
+			 * starts when the port is back in SNK_READY.  When the
+			 * request has to wait, the discover work retries it.
+			 */
+			if (tcpm_request_dfp_as_sink(port) <= 0)
+				mod_send_discover_delayed_work(port, 0);
 		} else {
 			port->send_discover = false;
 			port->send_discover_prime = false;
@@ -5904,6 +5991,15 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcp
 		port->nr_sink_caps = 0;
 		port->send_discover = true;
 		port->send_discover_prime = false;
+		/*
+		 * A new contract follows: ask for DFP again if that is due.
+		 * With tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink, drop a state change that was
+		 * queued before the reset: a request left there would go out
+		 * unchecked at the next SNK_READY.
+		 */
+		port->sink_dfp_done = false;
+		if (port->tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink)
+			port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
 		if (port->pwr_role == TYPEC_SOURCE)
 			tcpm_set_state(port, SRC_HARD_RESET_VBUS_OFF,
 				       PD_T_PS_HARD_RESET);
@@ -6050,6 +6146,7 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcp
 	/* DR_Swap states */
 	case DR_SWAP_SEND:
 		tcpm_pd_send_control(port, PD_CTRL_DR_SWAP, TCPC_TX_SOP);
+		port->send_discover_before_swap = port->send_discover;
 		if (port->data_role == TYPEC_DEVICE || port->negotiated_rev > PD_REV20) {
 			port->send_discover = true;
 			port->send_discover_prime = false;
@@ -6067,12 +6164,19 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcp
 		break;
 	case DR_SWAP_SEND_TIMEOUT:
 		tcpm_swap_complete(port, -ETIMEDOUT);
-		port->send_discover = false;
+		/*
+		 * With tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink a DR_Swap can precede
+		 * discovery, which is then still due when it got no answer.
+		 */
+		port->send_discover = port->tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink &&
+				      port->send_discover_before_swap;
 		port->send_discover_prime = false;
 		tcpm_ams_finish(port);
 		tcpm_set_state(port, ready_state(port), 0);
 		break;
 	case DR_SWAP_CHANGE_DR:
+		/* Whoever asked for it, a completed swap settles the data role */
+		port->sink_dfp_done = true;
 		tcpm_unregister_altmodes(port);
 		if (port->data_role == TYPEC_HOST)
 			tcpm_set_roles(port, true, TYPEC_STATE_USB, port->pwr_role,
@@ -7090,8 +7194,22 @@ unlock:
 static void tcpm_send_discover_work(struct kthread_work *work)
 {
 	struct tcpm_port *port = container_of(work, struct tcpm_port, send_discover_work);
+	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&port->lock);
+	/* Nothing to discover once the partner is gone, and no retry either */
+	if (port->tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink && !port->attached)
+		goto unlock;
+
+	/* A pending DR_Swap to DFP goes out before any Discover Identity. */
+	ret = tcpm_request_dfp_as_sink(port);
+	if (ret > 0)
+		goto unlock;
+	if (ret == -EAGAIN) {
+		mod_send_discover_delayed_work(port, SEND_DISCOVER_RETRY_MS);
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
 	/* No need to send DISCOVER_IDENTITY anymore */
 	if (!port->send_discover && !port->send_discover_prime)
 		goto unlock;
@@ -7109,6 +7227,8 @@ static void tcpm_send_discover_work(stru
 		goto unlock;
 	}
 
+	/* From here on tcpm_request_dfp_as_sink() makes no request */
+	port->sink_dfp_done = true;
 	tcpm_send_vdm(port, USB_SID_PD, CMD_DISCOVER_IDENT, NULL, 0, port->tx_sop_type);
 
 unlock:
diff --git a/include/linux/usb/tcpm.h b/include/linux/usb/tcpm.h
--- a/include/linux/usb/tcpm.h
+++ b/include/linux/usb/tcpm.h
@@ -130,6 +130,13 @@ enum tcpm_transmit_type {
  *		swap following Discover Identity on SOP' occurs.
  *		Return true when the TCPM is allowed to request a Vconn swap
  *		after Discovery Identity on SOP.
+ * @request_dfp_as_sink:
+ *		Optional; as Sink/UFP, request a DR_Swap to DFP once an explicit
+ *		contract is in place and before discovery, when the Source's
+ *		capabilities advertise data role swap. For controllers on which
+ *		a DR_Swap that the partner starts later does not hold. The
+ *		request is repeated after Wait and when it got no answer, with
+ *		a few requests per attach at most.
  */
 struct tcpc_dev {
 	struct fwnode_handle *fwnode;
@@ -148,6 +155,8 @@ struct tcpc_dev {
 	 */
 	bool (*consume_retained_sink_dfp)(struct tcpc_dev *dev);
 
+	bool request_dfp_as_sink;
+
 	int (*init)(struct tcpc_dev *dev);
 	int (*get_vbus)(struct tcpc_dev *dev);
 	int (*get_current_limit)(struct tcpc_dev *dev);
